WEBVTT

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.772
How they legislated death.

00:00:01.772 --> 00:00:05.626
This is the complete legislative record — every step that brought us here.

00:00:05.626 --> 00:00:07.590
February 2015.

00:00:07.590 --> 00:00:11.772
The Supreme Court of Canada rules unanimously in Carter v. Canada.

00:00:11.772 --> 00:00:17.181
The absolute prohibition on physician-assisted dying, they said, violates Charter rights.

00:00:17.181 --> 00:00:20.011
Parliament was given twelve months to write the law.

00:00:20.011 --> 00:00:21.693
June 2016.

00:00:21.693 --> 00:00:23.852
Bill C-14 passes.

00:00:23.852 --> 00:00:26.238
MAID is legalized — but with safeguards.

00:00:26.238 --> 00:00:29.147
Natural death must be reasonably foreseeable.

00:00:29.147 --> 00:00:31.863
A ten-day reflection period is mandatory.

00:00:31.863 --> 00:00:34.477
Two independent medical assessments are required.

00:00:34.477 --> 00:00:36.603
Those safeguards... would not last.

00:00:36.603 --> 00:00:38.943
September 2019.

00:00:38.943 --> 00:00:44.079
The Quebec Superior Court strikes down the foreseeable death requirement in Truchon v. Canada.

00:00:44.079 --> 00:00:46.159
The federal government does not appeal.

00:00:46.159 --> 00:00:51.295
Instead — and this is critical — they use the ruling to expand eligibility nationally.

00:00:51.295 --> 00:00:52.965
March 2021.

00:00:52.965 --> 00:00:54.977
Bill C-7 passes.

00:00:54.977 --> 00:00:56.727
The foreseeable death requirement?

00:00:56.727 --> 00:00:57.397
Gone.

00:00:57.397 --> 00:00:58.829
For all Canadians.

00:00:58.829 --> 00:01:04.352
Track 2 is created — MAID for chronic conditions, disabilities, and non-terminal illness.

00:01:04.352 --> 00:01:06.113
The ten-day reflection period?

00:01:06.113 --> 00:01:07.727
Eliminated for Track 1.

00:01:07.727 --> 00:01:11.306
You can now receive a lethal injection the same day you request it.

00:01:11.306 --> 00:01:17.568
Bill C-7 also included a sunset clause to expand MAID to people whose sole condition is mental illness.

00:01:17.568 --> 00:01:20.386
That expansion has been delayed three times.

00:01:20.386 --> 00:01:22.193
First to 2024.

00:01:22.193 --> 00:01:24.022
Then to 2025.

00:01:24.022 --> 00:01:25.806
Then to 2027.

00:01:25.806 --> 00:01:27.670
The repeated delays are telling.

00:01:27.670 --> 00:01:33.193
Even the government that wrote this legislation... keeps flinching from implementing its most extreme provision.

00:01:33.193 --> 00:01:34.534
They know what they've done.
